WEBVTT

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.800
I don't believe it.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.440
I did it.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.850
Huh? There's someone else here?

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.930
All right, I've decided!

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.780
What have you decided?

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.390
That's my special seat, you know.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.260
V..Vice President Jikukawa!

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.180
You're our new addition to
the student council, Miss...

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.690
Tamaki Chieno, the secretary.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.200
Just what is going on?

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.400
I'm quitting the student council.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.760
I think you noticed it as well, sir.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.160
Today's student council log.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.160
I miswrote the second character
in the word "perfect."

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.200
I wrote KABE instead of PEKI.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:04.960
Oh, you did?

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.010
Yes!

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.080
If I can make such an amateur mistake,
I'm unfit to be secretary.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.730
That's a shame.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.320
Losing you would be a shame.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.290
Your writing is very pretty.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.330
The way you use words is beautiful.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.400
What you write is very easy to read.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.730
Losing you would be a shame.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.990
So, don't say that you're quitting.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.810
Lost

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:05.930
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.850
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.730
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.110
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.820
Found

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.030
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.540
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.330
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.460
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:34.800
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.670
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.380
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:40.760
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.970
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:45.350
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.810
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.520
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.350
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:55.190
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.360
It's now or never

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.440
That is what they say

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.530
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:04.200
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.370
That is what they say

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.540
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.040
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.250
That is what they say

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.670
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:20.970
Darkness of the Heart

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.210
What is this?

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.430
Where's the president?

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:35.770
Tamaki Chieno likes Souji Jikukawa.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.410
You seem troubled, young lady.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.290
Who are you?!

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:49.040
Still, he is absorbed with Kaito Daimon.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.300
He won't even look at you.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:53.870
How sad, Miss Tamaki Chieno.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.330
Kaito Daimon should just
disappear for good.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.810
Who are you?

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.180
You're not one of our students, are you?

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.030
What are you doing on campus?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.480
Do you want to get rid of him?

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.340
Of Kaito Daimon?

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.160
I give this to you.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.500
Wh..What are you doing?!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:36.500
It's a charm to get back
the man that you love.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.490
Kaito Daimon, you will fight me.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.310
Via puzzles.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.010
Chieno...

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.660
What are you doing here?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.990
She's one of us.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.660
Of the Orpheus Order.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.450
What was that?!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:20.220
What's the meaning of this, Chieno?

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.360
Let's go, Kaito.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.640
The puzzle is in there.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.190
Hey! Don't just go
decidin' things for me!

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.840
Kaito Daimon alone may
challenge the puzzle.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:37.660
No one else is allowed to interfere.

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.940
Chieno...

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.290
I think you'd better move quickly.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:50.910
If you refuse the Puzzle of Judgment,
or cannot solve it...

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.950
That building will end up
like the puzzle just now.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.090
You can't! My laboratory's in there!

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.670
My studio!

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:07.170
Ah! My school lunches!

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.340
"Our school!" is what
you should be saying!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.720
You're a bunch of morons!

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.930
I swear! You all just
think about yourselves!

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.430
Can't you think about this school-

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.610
Wait right there!
Can't you think about this school-

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.210
We can meet again soon enough.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.240
If you solve the Puzzle
of Judgment, that is.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.540
Puzzle of Judgment, my ass!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.220
Why do I and the vice
president have to...

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:41.920
You shall continue to be
betrayed by those you trust

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.790
as you are challenged by the Game.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.260
Just what does this mean?

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.550
I'm gonna see for myself!

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.560
I don't know what the Orpheus
Order is about, but...

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.700
I'll do it.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:02.560
To find out why they'd do
this, what it's all for!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.480
Ah, Kaito!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.480
Don't go gettin' killed.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:22.580
It's Game time.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:25.190
That puzzle earlier...

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.090
If his friends hadn't made
it in time, he'd be dead.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.180
Kaito Daimon...

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:33.930
The way he is now, is he
really suited for the Game?

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:37.200
I'm about to show you.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.810
Kaito's true abilities, that is.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.430
Let's play up.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.660
You're late, Daimon.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.300
Take the escalator there to the
third floor hallway, please.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.180
I'll explain the rules.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:20.900
The 3rd to 7th floors comprise a

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.690
combative-type maze puzzle.

00:08:25.590 --> 00:08:28.530
As of now, you will be
heading for the goal,

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.280
which is the elevator hall on the 7th floor.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.620
Each division within the building

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:37.280
is a maze portioned by fire doors.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:47.250
Maze patterns are of A, B and C types.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.550
I will be changing the
patterns from here.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.910
It will take about ten seconds
for the fire doors to

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.550
open and close between pattern changes.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:02.120
If you become trapped between doors

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.810
and are unable to get out, you lose.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:08.630
If you're able to navigate the doors

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:13.820
and make it to the elevator hall
on the 7th floor, you win.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.070
That's what makes a combative-type
maze puzzle, huh?

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.550
A maze that can be endlessly
changed and altered...

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.990
If you don't remember the patterns and

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:25.860
stay two or three steps ahead of your opponent,

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:28.040
you'll never get out.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.840
Vice President, promise me something.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:37.190
If I win, you'll explain why you've
joined up with those guys!

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:39.220
Fine.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.560
Puzzle time, let's begin!

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.060
Daimon...

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.140
Article 7, Paragraph 1 of
Root Gakuen's school rules:

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:53.450
Running inside school
buildings is prohibited.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:54.830
School rules?!

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.380
Jeez! You're really pissing me off!

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:08.640
Switching multiple routes at once?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.170
You gotta be kidding me!

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:19.760
Article 1, Paragraph 1 of
Root Gakuen's school rules:

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.960
Taking the stairs two
at a time is forbidden!

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:23.920
Screw that!

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.740
This puzzle is a tough one!

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:42.320
The vice president was able to
make something like this?!

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:46.180
Is she really with those
people from before?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.680
When the hell did they
even make this puzzle?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:05.190
Just why are you doing this?

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:09.100
Chieno, are you really...

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:11.650
Switching to Maze Pattern A.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:28.580
The goal is up ahead.

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.100
It doesn't matter if it's
Pattern B or Pattern C:

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.590
if this shutter starts
to open, I've gotta go!

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:37.340
Switching to Maze Pattern B.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.340
Okay!

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.920
It's Pattern B! Can I make it?!

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.220
I couldn't make it!

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.480
Switching to Pattern C.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:56.240
Oh, no! I'm gonna get trapped!

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:05.450
Ah, looks like he escaped.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:12.130
You still haven't done all that you're
capable of, Tamaki Chieno.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:15.550
Try letting loose a little more.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:17.580
Be self-indulgent.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.280
Be self-righteous.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.950
Be selfish!

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:23.720
Otherwise, you won't beat Kaito Daimon.

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:35.210
I get it!

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.840
If I beat him with this puzzle,

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.070
Daimon will go away, won't he?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.570
Of course.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:47.060
That's the whole reason
I'm helping you guys.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.330
He will, of course, disappear...

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.830
from this world.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.400
The values suddenly began to increase.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.960
Amazing.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.800
Brainwave activity jumped at once to 89%.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.360
It's just strange, somehow.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:24.530
Something wasn't right with
the vice president earlier.

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:31.120
I've got it!

00:13:37.010 --> 00:13:39.130
What the hell?! I'm busy!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:42.600
I've got it! I know what's different
about the vice president!

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:43.760
Huh?

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.880
It's that earring!

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.370
The vice president's earring?

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:05.280
Article 3, Paragraph 1 of
Root Gakuen's school rules:

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:10.080
Piercings, earrings, rings and
other adornments are strictly forbidden.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.900
There's no way someone as upright as the

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:13.700
vice president would go breaking the school rules.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:15.210
An earring?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.420
Kaito Daimon, you will fight me.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.710
It's the same as the Armlet of Orpheus!

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.160
That's right, I think so too.

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.760
But I've never heard of an Orpheus Ring

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.760
in the form of an earring!

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:38.210
Actually, I think I get it somehow.

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:42.190
I've worn an Armlet of
Orpheus, so I get it.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:48.240
Your thinking, your emotions,
everything changes.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:52.740
Campus Puzzle Competition
Top Prize
Tamaki Chieno

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:56.250
It's a good puzzle.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:15:01.020
She's tough, and by-the-numbers
and complains a lot,

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:05.750
but the puzzles she makes are
true and straightforward.

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:06.970
They're pretty.

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.770
There's no way someone who could
make a puzzle like this

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:20.210
would hook up with guys
who'd destroy the school!

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:28.530
The earring is what's made
the vice president act weird!

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:31.260
Then, don't that make things bad?

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:33.750
If an Armlet of Orpheus runs wild,

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:37.200
the brain of the person wearing it
will encumber great strain.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.500
The vice president...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:39.730
She's in trouble!

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.030
Nonoha!

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.490
Kaito, please!

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:45.920
You have to get that earring off of her!

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:48.670
That was my plan before
you'd even told me!

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.210
You can't seem to trap him, can you?

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:54.400
At this rate, we won't be
able to get rid of him.

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:55.800
Of Kaito Daimon.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.610
You're fine not being
able to get him back?

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:00.950
Your precious Souji Jikukawa?

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:04.980
No! Anything but that...

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:05.770
No!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:19.280
Souji, see me. See only me!

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:24.120
Dammit!

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.380
Switching to Pattern B.

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:32.000
96... 97...

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:35.890
Forced activation rate has cleared 98%!

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.080
Incredible!

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:38.540
These numbers are only possible

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.200
because Kaito is our opponent.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.290
It was no mistake that you were chosen

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.190
as our opponent for the Game, Kaito.

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:04.710
The 7th Floor elevator
hall is just past here!

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:09.780
The goal is past there.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.670
This time for sure, I shall trap you.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.130
Ain't no way I'm gonna lose!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.700
I've already said I'm gonna
solve all deadly puzzles!

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.560
Switching to B.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:28.650
Here goes!

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:35.020
Kaito Daimon will not make it.

00:17:35.020 --> 00:17:39.300
If I change to Pattern C as
he's en route, I will win.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.410
Switching to C.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:49.000
Sure enough, you've continually
switched maze patterns!

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:53.920
The shutters pause for 0.5 seconds
every time you switch.

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:55.920
That's the moment of truth!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:08.250
I've solved it; I beat the puzzle!

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.460
He could read my movements.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:24.080
Forced activation has ceased.

00:18:25.390 --> 00:18:27.210
So that's it, eh?

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:44.750
Vice President!

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.980
That earring...

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.730
I... I...

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:00.150
Vice President!

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.200
Over there!

00:19:07.490 --> 00:19:08.690
Chieno!

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.080
Hang in there, Chieno!

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:17.880
President...

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:24.560
I don't want to quit the student council.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:30.150
But to lose control of
one's own emotions...

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:32.590
I'm unfit to be vice president.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.430
I don't understand.

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:38.090
Why would I do this?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.410
It would be a shame.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.290
To lose you, that is.

00:19:48.010 --> 00:19:50.200
The Monday conferences...

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.090
The Wednesday moral guidance...

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.920
The Friday student council minutes...

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:58.300
Oh, and today's school bus direction.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:03.140
Everything has gone well thanks to you,
Miss Vice President.

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.060
Mr. President!

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:12.100
So, don't say that you're
quitting, Tamaki.

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:14.180
Upperclassman!

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.610
You're not the one to blame here.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.490
The ones who used you are.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:31.650
She did some good work for us.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:35.140
Forced brainwave activity reached 98%!

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:39.760
Her desire to beat Kaito
had an effect on the Ring.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.760
Thank you, Tamaki Chieno.

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:46.010
We've collected some splendid
data thanks to you!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:47.760
"Data," you say?

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.370
Where the hell do you get off?!

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:53.020
Using ordinary people for crap like this!

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:56.670
What if something had happened
to the vice president?!

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:58.820
We don't care about that.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:02.700
All we want is our data, nothing more.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:08.490
We of the Orpheus Order
embrace the great Orpheus,

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.960
and seek to free man from

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:13.460
the yoke of the lesser gods.

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.740
Kaito Daimon, you who of his own will

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:17.740
abandoned an Armlet of Orpheus...

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:19.700
You are the enemy of mankind,

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.960
one who has rejected the possibility of evolution.

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:24.980
Kaito, going forward, you shall be

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:27.720
joining us on our Games.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.850
"Games," you say?!

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.660
And now for our next Game.

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:37.070
Wait there, asshole!

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:52.350
At this rate, maybe you won't
even be able to remember.

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:53.900
Me, that is.

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:55.040
What was that?!

00:21:58.970 --> 00:21:59.880
Bye-bye.

00:22:07.020 --> 00:22:09.240
Who the hell are those guys?

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:14.220
They're a gang who can make a
giant puzzle in a single day

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:17.420
and control people using
an Armlet of Orpheus.

00:22:18.030 --> 00:22:21.420
They're certainly different from the POG.

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.490
The Orpheus Order...

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.490 --> 00:24:04.090
Yeah, yeah, Airi, Airi!

00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:06.660
Yeah, yeah, Airi, Airi!

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:08.800
Next up, the puzzle that Miss Airi

00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:10.970
has kept hidden moves into play!

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:13.230
What's suddenly gotten
into that Mizutani chick?

00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:14.240
Gammon, you fool!

00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:16.060
Call her Miss Airi!

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:18.300
Oh, no! Now we've gotta go to

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:20.430
the sea to see what Miss Airi's seen!

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.850
Next time, "The Flip-Flop Trap"

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:26.630
The Flip-Flop Trap

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.550
Yeah, yeah, Airi, Airi!

00:24:24.550 --> 00:24:27.570
Yeah, yeah, Airi, Airi!
